    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane containing the line
<m>\mathbf r = \langle 3, 0, 2\rangle + t
\langle -4, 8, -4\rangle</m>
which is parallel to the plane <m>-4x  - 3y  - 2z = -21</m> in
which the coefficient of x is -4.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4\mathopen{}\left(x-3\right)+\left(-3\right)\mathopen{}\left(y-0\right)+\left(-2\right)\mathopen{}\left(z-2\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
